{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Files a SUBTASK under a running kb.plan item - the decomposition door for plan autonomy (owner, 2026-11: a task in progress may create subtasks and run them without waiting for a human). The parent's human acceptance authorizes its subtasks, so a subtask may be born `accepted` (runnable at once; the worker runs it before the parent) or `in-progress`, or `proposed` (queued behind an earlier sibling; the parent's coordination turn promotes it later with move_item). Inputs: parent = the EXACT claim of an accepted or in-progress, unpaused plan item; claim = a unique, self-contained sentence naming the subtask's outcome; detail = its own scope plus the concrete check that verifies it (may be empty); lifecycle = accepted | in-progress | proposed (empty = accepted). Refuses an unknown/proposed/blocked/settled parent, a duplicate claim, a parent-chain cycle, depth beyond 4 levels below a top-level item, or more than 12 open subtasks per parent. Files through agent.archivist.remember (journaled, work:true, origin:subtask, tags plan,<lifecycle>); author is the session user, else 'executive'. Returns remember's FLAT result plus parent, lifecycle, depth, siblings_open. Once a parent has subtasks it becomes their coordinator: it waits while any subtask is accepted/in-progress and may close only after all are completed/done and it has verified the integrated result. Use agent.plan.add_item for top-level (human-proposed) work.","import":"","params":[{"name":"parent","type":"String"},{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"detail","type":"String"},{"name":"lifecycle","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"qizorr1a1acc07097r3fb","readers":[],"time":1794333754819,"username":"system","writers":[]}